  "summary": "Yes, the contract contains an anti-assignment clause prohibiting either party from assigning, pledging, or transferring the agreement without prior written consent, except in connection with a Change of Control.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "passage_id": 2,
      "quote": "10.11 Assignment. Neither party will have the right to assign, pledge or transfer all or any part of this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other, and any such purported assignment, pledge or transfer by a party without such prior written consent shall be void ab initio; provided, however, that either party may assign all or part of its rights and obligations under this Agreement in connection with a Change of Control (as defined in the Asset Purchase Agreement)."
